phase2/wrapper-harness, 32-bit, run inside the container. Three wrappers driven
through the same call sequence the gralloc modules make.

NOTE: this harness feeds gbm_import the geometry the shipped code *intends* to
pass (width = total_size). In the real cross-process path the width is 0 -- see
trace-debug.log. The harness is therefore a useful A/B for "does the rebuild match
the shipped binary", but it did NOT reproduce the true failure, and an earlier
version of the fix passed here while still failing on the device.

#################### 32-bit: /vendor/lib/libgbm_mesa_wrapper.so (shipped) ####
  alloc 4096x338 R8: ok  out_fd=8 out_stride=4096 map_stride=4096 modifier=0x0
  import as gralloc does: w=1384448 h=1 R8 stride=1280 (YV12 luma stride)
    import FAILED  <-- the bug: gralloc then maps a NULL bo
  control XRGB8888: alloc ok, import ok, map OK

#################### 32-bit: wrapper32_rebuilt.so (faithful rebuild) #########
  alloc 4096x338 R8: ok  out_fd=8 out_stride=4096 map_stride=4096 modifier=0x0
  import as gralloc does: w=1384448 h=1 R8 stride=1280 (YV12 luma stride)
    import FAILED  <-- identical to shipped, as required
  control XRGB8888: alloc ok, import ok, map OK

#################### 32-bit: wrapper32_fixed.so ##############################
  alloc 4096x338 R8: ok  out_fd=8 out_stride=4096 map_stride=4096 modifier=0x0
  import as gralloc does: w=1384448 h=1 R8 stride=1280 (YV12 luma stride)
    import ok
    map at s_width x 1                     OK
    map at camera dims 1280x720            OK
  control XRGB8888: alloc ok, import ok, map OK
